<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hadadezer of Zobah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">10th century BCE</span> · Also known as Hadadezer son of Rehob</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hadadezer son of Rehob was a king of Aram-Zobah, an Aramaean kingdom in the Beqaa valley and inland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, known from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Hebrew Bible</a>. According to the books of Samuel and Chronicles he led a coalition of Aramaean states with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariots</a> and forces reaching the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a>, but was defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">King David</a>. No contemporary inscription names him.</p></div>
